    "# Load libraries\n",
    "import numpy as np\n",
    "import math\n",
    "import matplotlib.pyplot as plt\n",
    "\n",
    "# Change degrees to radians\n",
    "pi=np.pi\n",
    "deg2rad=pi/180\n",
    "rad2deg=1/deg2rad"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 2,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Define the latitude dependent insolation\n",
    "def Q_lat(xs,L=1,S0=1354.0):    \n",
    "\n",
    "    return  L*(S0/4)*(1 - 0.241*( 3*np.square(xs) - 1 ))\n",
    " "
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 3,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Define the albedo function\n",
    "def albedo(T,jmx):\n",
    "    alb=np.ones(jmx)*0.3\n",
    "    k=np.argwhere(T<=-2)\n",
    "    alb[k]=0.6# recalculate albedo for snowline at T=-10C\n",
    "    return alb"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 4,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Define the heat diffusion function\n",
    "\n",
    "def D_lat(xs,D0=0.44):\n",
    "    return D0*np.ones(len(xs))"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## CO2 outgassing"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 5,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "CO2_initial = 300\n",
    "def outgassing(yr):\n",
    "    outgassing_yr = 0.0129\n",
    "    CO2 = CO2_initial + yr * outgassing_yr\n",
    "    return CO2\n",
    "# test\n",
    "\n",
    "# CO2 = outgassing(100000)\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "<div class=\"alert alert-success\">\n",
    "\n",
    "**TASK 1.8 - increase in greenhouse gases**:\n",
    "\n",
    "A cheap and simple way of introducing $CO_2$ forcing into the model is to adjust the model parameter $A$ by $\\Delta A$, where\n",
    "    \n",
    "$$\\Delta A = \\ -k \\ \\ln\\left(\\frac{\\text{CO}_2}{360\\text{ppmv}}\\right)$$\n",
    "    \n",
    "with $k=5.35\\ \\mathrm{W/m^2}$, and $\\text{CO}_2$ is the concentration of $\\text{CO}_2$ in ppmv. Thus an increase in atmospheric $\\text{CO}_2$ causes a decrease in the longwave emissions to space. During ice ages, records from ice cores show that $\\text{CO}_2$ varied between $200$ ppmv and $280$ ppmv. A doubling of $\\text{CO}_2$ from todays value would take it up to around $720$ ppmv. \n",
    "    \n",
    "**1.8.1**: Explore what changes these values would make to climate. Note any effect that the ice albedo feedback or $D$ has. You may find it instructive to estimate the climate sensitivity parameter $-1/ \\lambda$ from  $-1/ \\lambda\\sim -\\Delta T_\\text{mean} / \\Delta A $, using that $\\Delta Q=-\\Delta A$.\n",
    " \n",
    "</div>"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 6,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Define the CO2 forcing function ( new A & B)\n",
    "\n",
    "def greenhouse(CO2):\n",
    "    ratioc = np.log(CO2 / 300)\n",
    "    A_kelvin = -326.4 + 9.161*ratioc - 3.164*ratioc**2 + 0.5468*ratioc**3\n",
    "    B = 1.953 - 0.04866*ratioc + 0.01309*ratioc**2 - 0.002577*ratioc**3\n",
    "    A = A_kelvin + 273.15*B\n",
    "    return A, B\n",
    "\n",
    "#test\n",
    "# greenhouse(720)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Sea Ice thickness ( Hard snowball)\n",
    "\n",
    "Sea ice thickness strictly determined by geothermal flow\n",
    "$$\n",
    "\\Delta z = \\frac{k \\Delta T}{F_g}\n",
    "$$\n",
    "\n",
    "$\\Delta z$ is the sea ice thickness \n",
    "\n",
    "$\\Delta T$ is the temperature difference between the atmosphere and the seawater beneath the ice. Using todays value we have $-2^\\circ\\mathrm{C}$\n",
    "\n",
    "$k = 2.5\\ \\mathrm{W}\\cdot\\mathrm{m}^{-1}\\cdot\\mathrm{K}^{-1}$ is the thermal conductivity of ice\n",
    "\n",
    "$f_g = 2.5\\ \\mathrm{W}\\cdot\\mathrm{m}^{-2}$ is the geothermal flux"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 7,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
